## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-conscious OTCA design, multi-tenant residency, and deletion rights in a real-world, cross-region telemetry pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- PII redaction and tokenization at ingress
- Tenant opt-in/out governance and regional routing
- Immutable audit logs for compliance
- Deletion requests via tombstones with cross-region propagation
- End-to-end testing including opt-out, deletion, and reconciliation

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(event) {
  const e = {...event};
  if (e.payload?.email) e.payload.email = 'REDACTED';
  if (e.payload?.phone) e.payload.phone = 'REDACTED';
  return e;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate no PII leaks in dashboards across regions?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect deletion propagation delays?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design privacy-first OTCA paths that enforce data residency, tenant isolation, and masking, going beyond basic streaming.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA data contracts, regional immutable storage, global masked aggregates
- Per-tenant masking (tokenization, redaction) and tenant-key management
- Data lineage, access controls, and residency verification

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskRecord(record, tenantKey) {
  const masked = { ...record };
  if (masked.email) masked.email = hash(masked.email + tenantKey);
  if (masked.phone) masked.phone = redact(masked.phone);
  // redact other PII fields as needed
  return masked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test masking correctness and residency under synthetic bursts?
- How do you handle schema evolution for masked fields across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates ability to design data-rights enforcement in OTCA with cross-region flows and immutable stores.

## Key Concepts
- Deletion token propagation
- Tombstone and GC semantics for Kafka
- Immutable storage considerations (Parquet/S3)
- Auditability and legal holds
- Schema-versioning to avoid replay risks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: emit tombstone and propagate deletion token
function deleteTenantData(tenantId){
  emitKafkaTombstone(tenantId);
  purgeDerivedFeatures(tenantId);
  markParquetShardsDeleted(tenantId);
  updateCentralRegistry(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test deletion under concurrent deletion requests?
- How would you handle multi-tenant data that migrates regions after deletion?
